          "line_no": 177,
          "text": "In `django/http/request.py`, `HttpRequest.accepted_types` parses the `Accept` header into `MediaType` instances. When a client sends an `Accept` header containing tokens that trigger a `ValueError` du…"
        },
        {
          "line_no": 179,
          "text": "Currently, this `ValueError` is uncaught in `HttpRequest.accepted_types`, causing requests with malformed tokens to fail with an unhandled exception (HTTP 500 error) rather than safely discarding the …"
        },
        {
          "line_no": 182,
          "text": "1. Catches `ValueError` during token parsing in `HttpRequest.accepted_types` and safely skips invalid tokens, allowing valid media types in the header to be processed normally."
        },
        {
          "line_no": 183,
          "text": "2. Catches `ValueError` in `HttpRequest.accepted_type` and `MediaType.match` when matching against malformed input strings, returning `None` and `False` respectively."
        },
        {
          "line_no": 205,
          "text": "2026-11-27T07:41:47.4399058Z   PR_TITLE: Fixed #37542 -- Fixed unhandled ValueError from malformed tokens in HttpRequest.accepted_types."
